From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:33:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: sample the page's top color after each
 load
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Plan B45 (docs/arc-spec/06-flows.md §17.4, E18): the web toolbar takes the
rendered color at the top-right of the visible page, sampled once per
finished main-frame load (navigation, reload; at the scroll position of that
moment), not on scroll or later style changes; a classic scrollbar at the
right edge makes the shell use its neutral fallback instead.

openarc/browser/openarc_page_top_color.{h,mm}: PageTopColorSampler, a
WebContentsObserver. After a committed cross-document main-frame navigation
finishes loading, it measures the classic scrollbar's width in an isolated
world (innerWidth - scrollingElement.clientWidth), waits for a visual state
round trip, then copies a 3 x 12 DIP area at the view's top-right corner with
RenderWidgetHostView::CopyFromSurface, converts it to sRGB (the copy is in the
display's color space) and averages it. Hidden tabs are sampled when shown;
failed copies are retried a few times.

OACTabState gains pageTopColorKind / pageTopColor and the delegate
-tabDidSamplePageTopColor:. Without this patch the shell has no page color
and the toolbar can only show its neutral color.
